NEW_SECTION

<section>
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2><span class="num">02</span>Shipping a new release</h2>
        <p class="lede">
            Everything the engine fetches stays in <code>sessionStorage</code> — and that survives a
            reload, even a hard one. <code>config.cacheVersion</code> ties the cache to a release: when
            the value changes, the engine empties its cache and the next navigation fetches fresh.
            This page reads it from <code>/version.json</code> before <code>initialize()</code>.
        </p>
        <div class="release-grid">
            <div>
                <div class="panel">
                    <div class="panel-h"><span>try it</span></div>
                    <div class="panel-b">
                        <ol class="steps">
                            <li>Click <b>User 7</b> — fetched, so the progress bar shows.</li>
                            <li>Click it again from another route — served from cache, no bar.</li>
                            <li>Ship a release: type a new version below and set it, or edit
                                <code>examples/spa/version.json</code> on disk and press <b>Check</b>.</li>
                            <li>Click <b>User 7</b> — the bar is back: the cache was emptied.</li>
                        </ol>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="panel">
                    <div class="panel-h"><span>release controls</span></div>
                    <div class="panel-b">
                        <div class="field">
                            <label class="lbl" for="verInput">config.cacheVersion <span class="val" id="verLive">–</span></label>
                            <div class="row">
                                <input type="text" id="verInput" style="flex:1; min-width:0" spellcheck="false">
                                <button class="primary" id="btnSetVer">Set</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="row">
                            <button id="btnCheck">Check /version.json</button>
                            <button class="danger" id="btnClear">clearCache()</button>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="status" id="relStatus"><span class="dot"></span><span>waiting for boot</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="panel">
                    <div class="panel-h"><span>sessionStorage, live</span></div>
                    <div class="panel-b">
                        <table id="cacheTable">
                            <thead><tr><th>key</th><th>entries</th><th>holds</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody></tbody>
                        </table>
                        <p class="note" style="margin-top:12px">
                            <code>vuxSpaLoads</code> is this page's own key: <code>clearCache()</code>
                            empties only the engine's four, so app state — like auth in
                            <code>userProperties</code> — survives a release.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="panel">
                    <div class="panel-h"><span>in your app</span></div>
                    <pre class="snip">const res = await fetch("/version.json", { cache: "no-store" });
spa.config.cacheVersion = (await res.json()).build;
spa.initialize();

// later, on a live engine: clears at once if it changed
spa.config.cacheVersion = newBuild;</pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

